  "description": "MiaAI-Lab Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Dual-DGX-Sparks on two GB10 Sparks: vLLM TP2 with expert parallelism and MTP=3 speculative decoding, fp8 KV, bf16 mamba SSM state, 262,144 native context (YaRN x4 reaches ~1M but costs draft acceptance). Reduced-vocabulary MTP drafting is the largest single decode lever: the drafter carries its own BF16 lm_head over the full 248,320-token vocabulary, and slicing it shrinks the per-step read. Measured single-stream decode is strongly workload-dependent because speculative acceptance is: 39.9 tok/s on prose (35.2% accept), 57.3 on code (67.7%), 68.5 on structured counting (87.1%), at a flat ~52 ms step time across all of them. Vision and video inputs both verified end to end.",
